# docs/assets-plan.md. An IMAGE, because iOS depth-stubs
# `expect_typeface` and iOS is the lane whose asset delivery IS the
# shipped packaging mechanism. THE PICTURE IS SCENERY (the images/
# family, whose README says why): the DECLARED mark is a user-supplied
# source of any size and an image widget's intrinsic size drives layout,
# so this scene reports the mark's bytes as PRESENT and shows the small
# one. THE MISS SENTENCE names what the package
# CARRIES, so it passes only on a lane that staged the WHOLE root
# (tools/check-assets.py holds it equal to that root's listing), and its
# quoted `;` is the wall holding the three statement splitters equal.
expect label#0 "assets"
expect image#0 "2x2"
expect label#1 "kaya: no asset named "icons/nope.png"; the package carries fonts/OFL.txt, fonts/README.md, fonts/sora-wght.ttf, icons/README.md, icons/kaya-mark.png, identity.toml, images/README.md, images/a11y-logo.png, market/README.md, market/prices.csv, market/transactions.csv, win/README.md, win/minimal-resources.pri"
# 111400 is the vendored font's WHOLE size, so a reader that truncated
# into a fixed buffer fails here. "no complaint" is the query's positive
# answer (the empty string) rendered.
expect label#2 "icons/kaya-mark.png present, fonts/sora-wght.ttf: 111400 bytes, no complaint"
